@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk User Detail Update Integration
	Testing user detail sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the users with the following screen names from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1 |
	| osb.customer2 |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken    |
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View user updates
	OSB user updates to detailson web should sync properly to Zendesk.

	Given I log into the web homepage as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the privacy policy form
	And I update my details as "osb.customer1" to the following values
	| Email Address | edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Edit                             |
	| Last Name     | User1                            |
	And I log out and log into the web homepage as "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the privacy policy form
	And I update my details as "osb.customer2" to the following values
	| Email Address | edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Edit                             |
	| Last Name     | User2                            |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	Then the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the uuid of the web user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "edit.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Edit User1"
	And the user with the email address "edit.user2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Edit User2"